  "summary": "Retired and this is under revision.\n\n➢\tLong-term operations background; highly focused on constantly ensuring safety in all environments, with a strong belief that proactive measures will result in a zero-incident workplace with reduced costs and improvement in bottom line performance.\n➢\tOffer proven experience in chemical production, construction and processing industries; exceptionally knowledgeable in industrial safety, manufacturing/production and staff training; in-depth experience in operation of Gas Generators, Heaters, Distillation, Dryers, Steam and Hot Oil systems as well as Gas/Steam Turbines, Pumps/Compressors and Reactors, among others.\n➢\tHighly knowledgeable in hazardous materials handling, including NGLs, Acids/Caustics and Hydrocarbons.\n➢\tConsidered to be Subject Matter Expert in tracing process pipelines, identifying problems and slashing related costs; additional familiarity with use of Piping and Instrument Diagrams (P&IDs) walkdowns/punchlists, new plant commissioning/startup, safety audits and writing procedures.\n➢\tContributed subject matter expertise along with dynamic communication skills toward delivering quality operations courses at College of the Mainland for Union Carbide; OSHA Authorized Trainer for General / Construction Industry.\n➢\tParticularly adept in drafting and revising corporate procedures.\n➢\tHighly productive in achieving organizational objectives; rapidly learn and/or adapt to new operational methodologies and procedures; most recently have developed PowerPoint presentations related to Energy and Safety and developed database charting systems.",
